.TH IDERM 1 "2026-08-16" "IDERM 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iderm \- project intelligence in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iderm
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm scan --format=json
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm doctor --json
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm ledger record
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ "--note " text ]
.br
.B iderm ledger diff
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm ledger --json
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm graph
.RB < --dot | --mermaid >
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm ai repair
.RI [ path ]
.RI [ --apply ]
.br
.B iderm ai explain
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm ai test
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm trust
.RI [ path ]
.br
.B iderm --version
.RB | " -V"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iderm
scans a project, runs Doctor checks, and opens a terminal workspace.
It can also expose the same project model through headless commands.
.PP
The default
.I path
is the current directory.
Startup performs local scanning and Doctor evaluation. Core does not require
network access.
.SH HEADLESS COMMANDS
.TP
.B scan --format=json
Print detected manifests, language data, and compile database entries in a
versioned JSON envelope. This command does not write project state.
.TP
.B doctor --json
Print built-in and project-local Doctor findings in a versioned JSON envelope.
This command does not write project state.
.TP
.B ledger record
Scan the project and append one record to
.IR .iderm/run-ledger.jsonl .
The optional
.B --note
value is stored as unparsed text.
.TP
.B ledger diff
Print a structural JSON diff of the two newest ledger entries. At least two
entries are required.
.TP
.B ledger --json
Print all ledger entries in recording order. A missing ledger produces an
empty list.
.TP
.B graph --dot
Print the build graph as DOT text.
.TP
.B graph --mermaid
Print the build graph as Mermaid text.
Graph data is derived from a real
.IR compile_commands.json .
No compile database produces empty output.
.TP
.B ai repair
Send project and Doctor state to the external command declared by
.IR .iderm/ai.toml .
Without
.BR --apply ,
print proposals only. With
.BR --apply ,
create accepted new files after path validation.
.TP
.B ai explain
Request an external explanation of Doctor findings.
.TP
.B ai test
Run the one derived task whose label contains
.B test
and pass its output to the configured external command. Refuses and names
every candidate if more than one task matches.
.TP
.B trust
Review and approve every declared, gate-covered file the project currently
has --
.IR .iderm/ai.toml ,
.IR .iderm/tasks.toml ,
any auto-discovered
.I stream_*
script, and any project-local
.IR .iderm/languages/*.toml
-- prompting once per file. The explicit, non-interactive-safe way
to establish trust ahead of a scripted or CI run. See
.BR iderm-security (7).
.TP
.B --version, -V
Print the version and exit.
.SH TREE KEYS
.TP
.BR Up , " Down" , " j" , " k"
Move selection.
.TP
.BR PageUp , PageDown
Scroll Doctor findings.
.TP
.BR Home , End
Select the first or last tree item.
.TP
.B /
Search tree text.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected file in Neovim.
.TP
.B s
Suspend the workspace and start
.BR $SHELL .
.TP
.B r
Open Repair. Use
.B y
to apply,
.B n
to skip, or
.B Esc
to cancel.
.TP
.B b
Toggle build tree.
.TP
.B g
Toggle Git status.
.TP
.B x
Toggle task list.
.TP
.B o
Open the Rust outline.
.TP
.B p
Preview Markdown.
.TP
.B v
View SVG.
.TP
.B i
Inspect JSON or YAML.
.TP
.B w
Open the workbench picker.
.TP
.B l
Start an LSP handshake in the background.
.TP
.B t
Toggle dense and CRT themes.
.TP
.BR q , Esc
Close the active panel, or exit from the tree.
.SH WORKBENCH KEYS
.TP
.B F5
Toggle live refresh. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+l .
.TP
.BR F6 , F7
Decrease or increase refresh interval. Alternatives:
.B Ctrl+,
and
.BR Ctrl+. .
.TP
.B F8
Add a pane. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+a .
Up to four panes are supported.
.TP
.B F9
Export the focused XY chart as SVG and TikZ. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+e .
.TP
.B Insert
Snapshot the focused table. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+i .
.TP
.B Shift+F5
Toggle live refresh for all panes. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+Shift+l .
.TP
.BR Shift+F6 , Shift+F7
Decrease or increase refresh interval for all panes. Alternatives:
.B Ctrl+Shift+,
and
.BR Ctrl+Shift+. .
.TP
.B Shift+F10
Snapshot all tables. Alternative:
.BR Ctrl+Shift+i .
.TP
.B Tab
Select the next pane.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the workbench.
.PP
The workbench accepts free text. Therefore
.B q
is input, not a close key.
.SH TASKS
One-shot tasks receive terminal handover and run to completion.
Continuous tasks run in the background. Selecting the same continuous task
again stops it. IDERM stops remaining continuous children on exit.
.PP
Root files named
.BI stream_ name .py
or
.BI stream_ name .sh
are discovered as continuous tasks. The output argument is
.IB name .analog-capture .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .iderm/
Project-local configuration and generated state.
.TP
.I .iderm/run-ledger.jsonl
Append-only Run Ledger.
.TP
.I .iderm/exports/
SVG and TikZ figure exports.
.TP
.I logs/
Continuous-task logs.
.PP
See
.BR iderm-config (5)
for the complete layout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SHELL
Shell started by the
.B s
action. If unset, IDERM uses
.IR /bin/sh .
.TP
.B PATH
Used to locate Git, Neovim, language servers, task programs, and the configured
AI command.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A recognized command failed, required input was invalid, or no interactive
terminal was available for TUI startup.
.SH SECURITY
Project plugins are sandboxed WASM components. Project tasks, Git, Neovim,
language servers, shells, and AI commands are native processes with the user's
permissions.
.PP
Inspect an unfamiliar project's
.I .iderm/
directory, build manifests, and
.B stream_*
scripts before executing project actions.
See
.BR iderm-security (7).
.SH NOTES
IDERM requires no login, cloud workspace, or animated assistant. If startup
enters a loop and produces 80 decibels, verify that you did not install an old
Cisco router by mistake.
.PP
Mouse input is additive. The keyboard remains fully supported. Darwin may
reconsider evolution after observing certain touch interfaces.
.PP
On some laptop keyboards
.B PageUp
and
.B PageDown
exist only as
.B fn+Up
and
.BR fn+Down ,
and some terminal applications do not translate that combination into the
expected escape sequence, so Doctor-panel scrolling has no effect. This case
has no in-app fallback chord; remap
.B fn+Up
/
.B fn+Down
to send real
.B Page Up
/
.B Page Down
at the operating-system or terminal level.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iderm-config (5),
.BR iderm-plugin (7),
.BR iderm-security (7),
.BR git (1),
.BR nvim (1)
